    "description": "## Summary\n\nWhen a Sign-Up's Status first becomes Completed, the system stamps the completion date/time on the Sign-Up — once, permanently.\n\n## Context\n\nPlayer status automation (BUILD-178 epic) turns on the moment a Sign-Up is completed, and the 90-day inactivity clock is measured from completion moments. Sign_Up__c has no field recording when Status became Completed — this story creates that timestamp. Prerequisite for every other story in the epic.\n\n## Current state\n\nSign-Up completion runs through the Screen_Sign_Up_Complete screen flow → Complete_Sign_Up autolaunched flow, which writes deposit/first-bet fields and Status\\__c — no timestamp. Status_\\_c can also be set to Completed directly by a data load.\n\n## Proposed solution\n\n1. NEW field Sign_Up\\__c.Completion_Date_\\_c — DateTime, read-only on layouts, help text: \"Set automatically when Status first becomes Completed.\"\n2. Stamp the field exactly once, at the moment Status first becomes Completed, covering **both** the screen-flow path and direct record updates/data loads. Suggested approach: a before-save record-triggered flow (Sign_Up_Before_Save_Stamp_Completion_Date) — it covers every path without touching Complete_Sign_Up. Developer may adjust the implementation if there's a better fit, as long as the acceptance criteria hold.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n1. Completing a Sign-Up via the screen flow or a data load/record update stamps the field, once.\n2. The value never changes after first stamp — editing a Completed record, or Archived → reactivated → Completed again, keeps the original.\n3. Status changes to any non-Completed value do not stamp.\n\n## Output\n\nField + flow deployed in Partial SB; API names recorded on this ticket; requirements doc updated.",
